     4	
     5	**Goal:** Build a Three.js browser game that simulates launching Estes-style model rockets into seeded, procedurally generated environments, with grounded-but-approachable physics, live telemetry, and light challenges.
     6	
     7	**Architecture:** A pure, framework-free simulation core (`src/sim/`) — RNG, motors, thrust curves, atmosphere, integrator, flight state machine, outcomes — is driven test-first with Vitest and imports no Three.js. A thin rendering/UI layer (`src/world/`, `src/ui/`, `src/audio/`) reads sim state one-way and never writes back. `main.ts` wires a `SimConfig` into a `Simulation`, advances it on a fixed timestep via an accumulator, and renders each frame.
     8	
     9	**Tech Stack:** TypeScript, Vite, Three.js (npm), Vitest. No backend; static output. Brave CDP (port 9222) for render/UI smoke tests.
    10	
    11	**Spec:** `docs/spec.md`
    12	
    13	## Global Constraints
    14	
    15	- Language: TypeScript, `strict: true`. `tsc --noEmit` must pass with zero errors.
    16	- `src/sim/**` and `src/data/**` MUST NOT import from `three`, `src/world/**`, or `src/ui/**`. The dependency is one-way: `sim → (nothing UI/render)`; `world`/`ui` read `sim`.
    17	- Physics constant: `g = 9.81 m/s²`. Fixed sim timestep: `DT = 1/120 s`.
    18	- Determinism: all *simulation* randomness flows through the seeded `mulberry32` RNG in `src/sim/rng.ts`. `Math.random()` is banned in `src/sim/**` and `src/data/**` (these must be reproducible). Cosmetic-only jitter in `src/world/**` (e.g. flame flicker) and the per-launch seed source in `src/main.ts` (`Date.now()`) may use non-seeded randomness — but the seed, once chosen, drives all sim randomness deterministically.
    19	- Rocket roster target: ~12 models in `src/data/rockets.ts`. Motor set: Estes classes A–E in `src/data/motors.ts`.
    20	- Coordinate convention: `y` is up (meters); ground plane is `y = groundHeight`.
    21	- Quality gate (all must pass before "done"): `npm run test` (vitest), `npm run typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`), `npm run build` (vite build). `npm run quality` runs all three.
